      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "600fd01ffa56e073d18294ac",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A lot of this sounds like the same key problems we've been calling out since late 2018 when they tried expanding the types of instances. Privacy is important, definitely, but it is poorly done for exactly the reasons stated here. \"User is online in a private world\" is a very unfriendly thing to see, and 3 of the 4 privacy options cause that (Friends Only, Invite+, Invite Only). Pretty sure a lot of the people I know that lost interest in VRC were influenced by this problem without realizing it. If instances could separately define \"who can see\" and \"who can join\" an instance, at least some of the mystery would decline, like \"Oh a theater world, maybe I'll request after all\".",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
