      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 16
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This post honestly says more about the types of friends you have rather than an actual issue. Also I feel like this post disrespects boundaries a bit?  Orange status was added so that people could pace their interactions, some people get way too much attention and wanted a way to be able to slow it down a bit. If all of your friends want to be in smaller groups or even just alone most of the time and you don't agree with that, then just get new friends who are more active man. I don't see this as a reason to ruin the game for other people who may have social anxiety and need to pace themselves with the amount of people they are around at a time. \nAlso I need to stress the importance of how useful a friend that may not be around as much can actually be. Sometimes its good to have a friend that you dont see as much, keeps things fresh. Just do you man, don't be afraid to make new friends either if you feel like you want more interaction. The distant friends are still there and still care about you, they just might be dealing with more than you realize.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
