  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-26T08:17:35.126Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is a perfect storm of problems making Orange status a detrimental to the function of the social list\n\n\n*********Failure of Functions*********\n-Invites don't work correctly and its imposible to know if the user is in their world or a friends world\n-4 separate online statuses layering ontop making it more annoying to manage with friends, friends+ invite+, invite etc.\n-Players only see \"user is in private world\"\n\n\n*********Psychological effects for orange status already exists within playerbase*********\n-users stay as orange status 24/7 and have reclusive effects to their socialness \"Only people I want can join me, if only I could see the their requests\"\n-players see orange status and say \"do I really want to waste time to request to join? Will they even let me in? are they not inviting me because I'm not friend enough? Why would I even want to join them, they're probably sleeping in vr/watching a movie, I don't know I can't see the world they're in\"\n-\"They're alway orange status why would I want to be friends if they don't want me joining\"\n\n\n*********Failure on Existing Infrastructure*********\n-Red status should have had notifications visible in the menu not the hud\n-Notification system is the problem\n--the Notifications being annoying is the problem with talking the status rather the players wanting to join\n-\"i'm getting spammed with notifications\" if the notifications weren't spammable or just showed as a single invite, there would be no need to hide the hud or menu notifications on red status, be like discord and let it exist but only let me see it if I look at it\n-Worlds still don't have the ability to change from invite to friends+, meaning a new instance must be made before being able to invite a user\n--if you are already in the middle of something like a movie or a match, you're not going to want to start a new session\n--\"oh events need them and really on them\" If the ability to change the session from Friends+ to Invite existed, there would be no need to ask every person to change to orange status, much less it means someone could decide not to do it and let people come into the event to troll\n--The person in charge is being able to have control of the session is more important than making sure everyone in the room is orange\n\n\n\nBlue Green and Red are all the statuses definitely needed. Orange is just the excuse to be antisocial in an already confusing mess that is the session privacy. It is a net negative that does not even work with a busted notification system that doesn't even send notifications. Its a detriment to player experience and the social experience. It is a waste of API calls and of time to pretend it isn't a problem.",
